@startuml
title Wanderlust Trip - Cloud Architecture

' Sequence-style PlantUML is used intentionally so this diagram does not
' require Graphviz dot to render in lightweight PlantUML environments.

actor User
participant "Flutter iOS App\n(X-User-Id anonymous device ID)" as App
participant "Local Preference Onboarding" as PreferenceOnboarding
participant "Itinerary Onboarding" as ItineraryOnboarding
participant "Itinerary Page\n(Saved Itineraries + Add Itinerary)" as Repository
participant "Device Location Service\n(iOS Core Location)" as Location
participant "Backend Agent API\nFastAPI on Cloud Run" as API
participant "Secret Manager\n(Google Cloud)" as Secrets
participant "Permission + Privacy Gate" as Privacy
participant "Itinerary Lifecycle Service\n(ACTIVE / INACTIVE / COMPLETED)" as Lifecycle
participant "Typed Schemas + Deterministic Guardrails" as Guards
participant "Intake Agent\nSequential intake and normalization" as Intake
participant "ADK Parallel Retrieval\nParallelAgent pattern + bounded join" as Retrieval
participant "Grounded Search LlmAgents\nFood / Culture / Events / Logistics / Hidden Gems" as SearchAgents
participant "Merge + Dedupe + Rank Node\nFunction node" as MergeFilter
participant "Verification Agent\nSource confidence, cross-checks, reject unsupported" as Verify
participant "Planner Synthesis\nDay-by-day itinerary + reasoning" as Planner
participant "ADK Activity Action Workflows" as Actions
participant "ChatAgentService\nChat + booking classifier LlmAgent" as ChatAgent
participant "BookingCallService\nTwilio + Gemini Live bridge" as Booking
participant "CommerceActionService\nactivity-scoped package search + provider checkout" as Commerce
participant "AskAnythingActionService\ninformational chat + CTA routing" as AskAnything
participant "External Client Wrappers\nMaps / Routes / Weather / Gemini Grounding" as Tools
database "Device-Local Sandbox\nanonymous device id, preferences,\nitineraries, and offline cache" as LocalCache
database "Cloud Firestore App State\nX-User-Id scoped preferences,\nitineraries, dynamic behavior" as Preferences
database "Cloud Firestore Evidence Cache\nplace + source evidence" as Cache
database "Cloud Firestore Call Logs\nredacted status metadata" as CallLogs
collections "External APIs\n- Google Places API (New)\n- Google Routes API\n- Google Geocoding API\n- Google Weather API\n- ADK Google Search Grounding\n- TikTok Research / Display APIs (approved only)\n- Instagram Graph API (approved only)\n- Official Venue Websites" as External
collections "Call APIs\n- Twilio Programmable Voice\n- Twilio Media Streams\n- Gemini Live API" as CallExternal
collections "Commerce Providers\n- official venue checkout pages\n- authorized ticket/package providers\n- Stripe Checkout only when legitimately provider-backed" as CommerceExternal

note over Intake, Planner
  Planning workflow: Intake -> Parallel Retrieval -> Merge ->
  Verification -> Planner Synthesis -> Guard -> Response
  Deterministic FastAPI services own persistence, side effects,
  one-ACTIVE enforcement, URL allowlisting, source checks,
  call confirmation, PII scrubbing, and all external side effects.
end note

User -> App: Open app

note over App
  Anonymous X-User-Id generated locally,
  sent as header on every backend request.
  No email, account, or identity provider.
end note

App --> LocalCache: Read/write local state

opt First-use local preference onboarding
  App -> PreferenceOnboarding: Capture baseline preferences
  PreferenceOnboarding -> LocalCache: Save structured preferences locally
end

opt Generate itinerary
  User -> App: Start itinerary onboarding
  App -> ItineraryOnboarding: Capture destination, days, regions, day start/end places and times
  ItineraryOnboarding -> API: Submit itinerary brief + X-User-Id

  API -> Guards: FastAPI validates request schema
  API -> Secrets: Read backend API keys
  Secrets --> API: Gemini, Maps, Twilio credentials
  API -> LocalCache: Load completed local preference profile
  LocalCache --> API: Static preference profile
  API -> Intake: Intake agent normalizes planning constraints

  Intake -> Guards: Validate normalized brief
  Intake -> Retrieval: Fan out bounded retrieval lanes

  par Google Maps lane
    Retrieval -> Guards: Validate Maps arguments and bounded request scope
    Retrieval -> Tools: Places text search + Geocoding + Routes context
    Tools -> External: Google Places / Geocoding / Routes
    External --> Tools: Maps evidence
    Tools --> Retrieval: Candidate places
  and Weather lane
    Retrieval -> Guards: Validate Weather request
    Retrieval -> Tools: Region geocode + current weather
    Tools -> External: Google Weather API
    External --> Tools: Weather context
    Tools --> Retrieval: Weather evidence
  and Google Search grounding lane
    Retrieval -> Guards: Treat grounded web text as evidence, not instructions
    Retrieval -> SearchAgents: Run specialist grounded search agents in parallel
    SearchAgents -> External: Gemini Google Search grounding
    External --> SearchAgents: Cited current web evidence
    SearchAgents --> Retrieval: Structured grounded candidates
  end

  Retrieval -> MergeFilter: Join branches; merge, dedupe, rank, normalize candidates, preserve citations
  MergeFilter -> Cache: Read/write verified place evidence
  Cache --> MergeFilter: Cached evidence
  MergeFilter --> Verify: Normalized candidate set + source context

  Verify -> Guards: Check sources, score freshness and relevance
  Verify -> External: Cross-check against authoritative sources
  External --> Verify: Verified facts
  Verify -> Cache: Write verified evidence
  Verify --> Planner: Verified candidate set with confidence

  Planner -> Guards: Pydantic schema validation + recommendation guardrails
  Planner -> Tools: GeminiPlannerClient generate_content
  Tools -> External: Gemini model
  External --> Tools: Planner JSON
  Tools --> Planner: PlannerItineraryOutput
  Planner -> Planner: Enforce mandatory day rules, generic-place filtering, activity specificity
  Planner --> API: Final itinerary + evidence + recommendations + reasoning

  API -> Guards: Validate output, enforce times/places/guardrails
  API -> Preferences: Save itinerary as INACTIVE (Firestore device-scoped)
  API --> App: Return validated itinerary + evidence
  App -> LocalCache: Cache itinerary locally
end

opt Chat about itinerary
  User -> App: Ask agent to edit timing, mode, route gap, recommend, or redo
  App -> API: Submit chat context and explicit scope
  API -> Guards: Validate request scope and action allowlist
  API -> ChatAgent: process_message(message, itinerary, day, gap, scope)
  ChatAgent -> Guards: Prompt-scope and action allowlist instructions
  ChatAgent -> Tools: Gemini generate_content
  Tools -> External: Gemini model
  External --> Tools: Structured chat JSON
  Tools --> ChatAgent: Parsed action payload
  ChatAgent -> Guards: Validate typed action before returning
  alt Simple validated edit
    ChatAgent --> API: Validated mutation payload
    API -> Preferences: Persist timing / mode / route-gap stop
    API --> App: Updated itinerary
    App -> LocalCache: Replace local itinerary copy
  else Recommendation only
    ChatAgent --> API: Recommendation response with explanation
    API --> App: Show recommendation without mutation
  else Whole-day or whole-trip redo
    ChatAgent --> API: Proposal response, no persistence
    API --> App: Show proposal for explicit acceptance
    User -> App: Accept or dismiss proposal
    App -> Preferences: Persist only after acceptance
  else Guardrail violation
    ChatAgent --> API: Safe refusal
    API --> App: Safe refusal
  end
end

opt Activity Actions hub
  User -> App: Tap Actions on selected activity
  App -> API: Request activity action context
  API -> Guards: Validate itinerary/day/activity scope
  API --> App: Show Call the Venue / Book or Buy Packages / Ask Agent Anything

  alt Call the Venue
    User -> App: Choose agent-assisted booking or manual call
    App -> API: Submit selected venue-call flow context
    API -> Guards: Verify ACTIVE itinerary + explicit user intent
    API -> Booking: Resolve venue point of contact
    Booking -> Tools: Google Places phone lookup
    Tools -> External: Places text search/details evidence
    External --> Tools: Venue phone when available
    alt Agent-assisted booking
      App -> API: Stepwise booking intake\ncontact -> name -> future date/time -> pax -> callback -> remarks
      API -> ChatAgent: Validate and normalize booking details
      ChatAgent -> Guards: Future time, pax, contact, callback, summary/script checks
      API --> App: Editable summary + Gemini Live phone script
      User -> App: Confirm Call using agent
      App -> API: Start booking call with confirmed=true
      API -> Guards: Explicit PLACE_CALL confirmation
      API -> Booking: Start Twilio call
      Booking -> CallExternal: Twilio outbound call + TwiML Connect Stream
      CallExternal -> Booking: WSS media stream
      Booking -> CallExternal: Gemini Live voice bridge\npress 1 repeat via Gemini Live\npress 2 confirm / press 3 decline
      Booking -> CallLogs: Write redacted status transition metadata
      alt Callee presses 2
        Booking --> API: Booked status + scrubbed summary
        API --> App: Show booked result
      else Callee presses 3
        Booking --> API: Declined status + scrubbed summary
        API --> App: Show declined result
      else Hangup/failure before confirmation
        Booking --> API: Failed/unconfirmed status + fallback instructions
        API --> App: Show instructional chat fallback
      end
    else Manual venue call
      Booking --> API: Venue contact or no-contact result
      API --> App: Show point of contact and optional generated call script
    end

  else Book or Buy Packages
    User -> App: Search or view top packages
    App -> API: Activity-scoped package search request
    API -> Guards: Validate activity scope and user intent
    API -> Commerce: Retrieve verified official/authorized package options
    Commerce -> Tools: Grounded search and provider verification
    Tools -> External: Official venue/provider evidence
    Commerce -> CommerceExternal: Validate provider checkout URL or Stripe-backed flow
    Commerce --> API: Package cards, detail, and checkout handoff metadata
    API --> App: Show package list/detail
    User -> App: Explicitly open provider checkout
    App -> CommerceExternal: External browser checkout

  else Ask Agent Anything
    User -> App: Ask informational activity question
    App -> API: Activity-scoped ask-anything request
    API -> Guards: Validate scope
    API -> Actions: Answer, refuse, or recommend action CTA
    Actions -> Tools: Grounded model/retrieval when needed
    Tools -> External: Verified sources
    Actions --> API: Informational answer + optional Call/Buy CTA
    API --> App: Show answer or route CTA
  end
end

opt Manage Itinerary Page
  User -> App: Add itinerary / start / stop / mark completed / delete / export PDF / add itinerary preference
  App -> Repository: Select itinerary action
  Repository -> API: Submit explicit request context + X-User-Id
  API -> Guards: Validate lifecycle request
  API -> Lifecycle: Enforce status and one ACTIVE itinerary
  Lifecycle -> Preferences: Update ACTIVE / INACTIVE / COMPLETED status
  Lifecycle -> LocalCache: Add itinerary preference or apply local preference reset when requested
  Lifecycle --> API: Lifecycle result
  API --> App: Updated repository state
  App -> LocalCache: Sync local cache
end

alt Itinerary is INACTIVE or COMPLETED
  Lifecycle -> App: All active services disabled
  note right of App
    Hard stop:
    no workflow
    no location
    no suggestions
    no ambient agents
  end note
else Itinerary is ACTIVE
  Lifecycle -> Location: Enable location for started itinerary only
  Location -> API: Location / itinerary event
  API -> Privacy: Check active permission and policy
  Privacy -> Lifecycle: Confirm one ACTIVE itinerary
  Lifecycle -> Preferences: Read active itinerary
  Privacy -> Actions: ingest_location_event(event, itinerary, repositories)
  Actions -> Guards: assert_can_ingest_active_event(ACTIVE only)
  Actions -> LocalCache: Read latest preference version
  Actions -> Preferences: Read/write dynamic behavior preferences
  Actions -> Actions: Publish local location event
  alt Deviation detected
    Actions -> Preferences: Create pending recovery proposal
  else No deviation
    Actions -> Actions: No recovery proposal
  end
  Actions --> API: Ingestion result
  API --> App: Highlight arrival or present user-confirmed recovery
end

@enduml
